Jesssica wrote:
> 
> Does this mean it's advisable to do the Mines before
> Sokoban with wizards, to get more daggers, better armor,

You will find armor also in the main dungeon, there's no need
to kindly ask that dwarf with his wielded mattock to pass over
his mithril to you. ;-)

But first of all it depends very much on your alignment whether
the inhabitants of the mines are mostly hostile or not.

> and a chance of buying protection earlier?  Usually
> the Mines are more entertaining, so I go down there first --
> but when I do the dagger toss in the mines I seem to end
> up standing on Elbereth, surrounded by monsters, with
> me being unable to pick up the old daggers because that
> would entail moving off Elbereth.

Exactly that's one reason (but, of course, it always depends!)
why to delay the mines; you can get surrounded too easily. And
the wizards defense to keep a pet in between him and a monster,
or the wizards attack means to throw daggers or cast spells
are much more effective in places where you can easily get many
monsters in straight line, like corridors.

But other conditions might even force you to enter the mines
early; lack of food, for example, in cases when you cannot yet
reach Sokoban.

I don't think that one can generally answer your question by a
single strategy, but every weak character is quite ineffective
and very vulnerable in a hostile mines environment.

